hard classification, rotator with durable state + rotation logging, App installation-token minter, pool resolves the current identity's credential at connection start). Two pieces remain before the github namespace fails over live:\n\n1. **Daemon call-path wiring**: when a `tools/call` result from the github server carries a GitHub API soft block (the error text embeds the API status/body), translate it to `mcpauth.APIError`, run the call through `Rotator.Do`, respawn the github instance with the rotated identity's env, and retry — so the calling session never sees the soft block. Hard blocks surface unchanged.\n2. **Live activation**: enroll the three GitHub App identities' private keys in the mcpx secret store (by name only), add the `failover` block to the github server's auth config with the user token last, and set the rotation state path.\n\nAcceptance: a staged low-limit identity in front of the real one shows a session-visible success on a forced soft block in the live namespace, with the rotation log line naming both identities; hard-block behaviour unchanged.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8017/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8017/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}